  "name": "Cypriot tsiattista (improvised dueling couplets)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Cypriot tsiattista improvised-couplet poetic-dueling tradition of Cyprus (Greek-Cypriot communities), Performance: two poet-singers face off in extempore Greek-Cypriot-dialect rhymed-couplet exchange, each turn answering the previous while introducing new poetic-and-philosophical-and-humorous-and-mocking material, accompanied by violin and laouto. The genre is structurally parallel to other improvised-poetic-dueling Mediterranean traditions (Basque bertsolaritza, Italian stornelli, Sardinian gara poetica, Sicilian mottetto), but with Cypriot-Greek dialect register and tetraposyllabos-fifteen-syllable-line characteristic poetic-meter. Performance contexts: weddings, agricultural festivals, and the annual Tsiattistakia festivals in Cyprus.",
